# Testing, Evaluation & Release Evidence

This is a **testing and evaluation evidence register**, not a claim that any initiative has completed production validation.

| Product | Known engineering/testing activity | Unverified or blocked evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Alyntara AI Agent | Voice, multilingual input, turn-taking, stop commands, API interactions, release-candidate and regression checks | Complete latest-SHA test run, reliable voice results, security/NFR gates and end-to-end demonstration |
| Alyntara Digital Twin | Focused task lifecycle, persistence, adapter and approval-state tests | Full regression suite, live external integrations, authorization checks and reachable demo |
| Cognitwist AI | Job discovery quality, role matching, UX and data source approaches under improvement | Reproducible relevance evaluation, integration tests and latest release acceptance |
| MOTWise | UI reviews, payment abstraction and subscription verification activities | Verified latest-SHA UI, end-to-end test-mode payments, security and owner acceptance |

Known risks remain: voice stability, unverified Digital Twin live integrations and MOTWise production charging, which must stay off pending explicit approval.

## Minimum evidence for a completed test run

- **Source:** repository, full commit SHA, component and release version.
- **Context:** UTC execution date, environment, configuration and synthetic test inputs.
- **Procedure:** commands, scenarios, acceptance thresholds and scope.
- **Results:** explicit passed, failed, blocked and not-run counts.
- **Proof:** CI URL, sanitised logs, trace/report and known defects.
- **Decision:** release gate and owner acceptance, if applicable.

## Proposed evaluation methodology

Define baseline scenarios → establish functional and safety criteria → run reproducible tests → review failures and response quality → re-run exact scenarios → report readiness for the exact commit.

No numerical test pass rate, model quality metric or production-readiness claim is made without published verification.

